 .SH OPTIONS
 .TP
 .B \-b
-dmenu appears at the bottom of the screen.
+accepted for compatibility; dmenu is always centred on the screen.
 .TP
 .B \-f
 dmenu grabs the keyboard before reading stdin if not reading from a tty. This
 is faster, but will lock up X until stdin reaches end\-of\-file.
 .TP
 .B \-i
-dmenu matches menu items case insensitively.
+dmenu matches menu items case insensitively (the default).
+.TP
+.B \-s
+dmenu matches menu items case sensitively.
 .TP
 .BI \-l " lines"
 dmenu lists items vertically, with the given number of lines.
@@ -61,8 +64,31 @@ from 0.
 .BI \-p " prompt"
 defines the prompt to be displayed to the left of the input field.
 .TP
+.B \-a
+app mode (dmenu_run uses it): commands with a desktop entry are listed first
+and can be found by their name, generic name, keywords and category (so
+"notes" finds a text editor); commands launched before move up. In the
+horizontal layout, desktop apps fill the first row and terminal apps,
+developer tools and other commands a dimmer second row; Up and Down switch rows.
+Extra tags are read from /etc/dmenu-greenleaf/tags and
+~/.config/dmenu-greenleaf/tags, one command per line followed by its tags,
+e.g. "mousepad notes notepad". Launch counts are kept in
+$XDG_CACHE_HOME/dmenu-greenleaf/history.
+.TP
 .BI \-fn " font"
-defines the font or font set used.
+ignored, so that a window manager's small bar font does not shrink the results.
+.TP
+.BI \-lfn " font"
+defines the font or font set used for the results.
+.TP
+.BI \-ifn " font"
+defines the larger font used for the prompt and text entry.
+.TP
+.BI \-pw " width"
+width in pixels of the centred search area.
+.TP
+.BI \-br " radius"
+blur radius of the darkened screen snapshot shown behind dmenu; 0 disables it.
 .TP
 .BI \-nb " color"
 defines the normal background color.
@@ -91,8 +117,12 @@ prints version information to stdout, then exits.
 .BI \-w " windowid"
 embed into windowid.
 .SH USAGE
-dmenu is completely controlled by the keyboard.  Items are selected using the
-arrow keys, page up, page down, home, and end.
+Typed text is split into space-separated keywords that may appear in any
+order. Each keyword matches an item as a substring or, failing that, as a fuzzy
+subsequence (e.g. "gerth" matches google-earth-pro); results are ranked by match
+quality. Items are selected using the arrow keys, page up, page down, home, and
+end, or with the mouse: hover to select, click to choose, scroll the wheel to
+move through the results. Clicking outside the results closes dmenu.
 .TP
 .B Tab
 Copy the selected item to the input field.
